# Addresses that moved, sent to where they went. Read by Cloudflare Pages at the edge.
#
# Nothing else serving `dist/` reads this unless taught to: `vite preview` serves it as a file.
# The browser tests run against a preview server taught these rules by `scripts/preview.config.ts`,
# the measure instrument's server (`scripts/serve-dist.ts`) reads them through the same parser, and
# `tests/e2e/redirects.spec.ts` visits every source below and checks it lands.
#
# Not every rule that deploys is here. An IRN or seat typed without its leading zeros (#596) is
# one rule per key, read off the feed, so the build appends those to `dist/_redirects` — see the
# `unpadded-addresses` integration in `astro.config.mjs`. `tests/dist/addresses.spec.ts` checks them.
#
# The incoming query is kept only when the destination names none of its own, so no destination
# here carries a `?` — the levers in an old scenario link are the part worth keeping.

# The reach view became the runner's second tab (#548).
/reach  /scenario/reach  301

# A district's scenario became the runner opened on that district (#548). The IRN rides in the
# fragment so the query, which holds the reader's levers, passes through untouched; the runner
# reads `#d=` and writes it back as `?d=`. See `chosenDistrict` in `src/lib/scenario.ts`.
/district/:irn/scenario  /scenario#d=:irn  301
